---
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import { OrganicDemo } from './react/product/OrganicDemo';
import { PerformanceDemo } from './react/product/PerformanceDemo';
import { AutomationDemo } from './react/product/AutomationDemo';

import headphones from '@/assets/demo/headphones.jpg';
import watch from '@/assets/demo/watch.jpg';
import sneakers from '@/assets/demo/sneakers.jpg';

const [h, w, s] = await Promise.all(
  [headphones, watch, sneakers].map((src) =>
    getImage({ src, width: 640, height: 640, format: 'webp', quality: 72 }),
  ),
);

const photos = [
  { key: 'headphones', src: h.src, alt: 'Black over-ear headphones on a yellow backdrop', label: 'Headphones' },
  { key: 'watch', src: w.src, alt: 'White smartwatch on a pale grey surface', label: 'Smartwatch' },
  { key: 'sneakers', src: s.src, alt: 'Pastel sneakers on a white plinth', label: 'Sneakers' },
];
---

<section id="product" class="bg-transparent py-16 md:py-32">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 md:px-6">
    <h2 class="max-w-3xl text-balance font-display text-h2 font-bold text-foreground">Data in. Better creative out.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[52ch] text-base text-muted-foreground md:mt-5 md:text-lead">
      Continuum reads how your posts and ads perform and makes the next creative from it: organic, then paid media on Meta, then production from your own design files. New ads ship paused.
    </p>

    <article id="organic" class="mt-12 md:mt-28 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="organic-title">
      <p class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-brand-violet">Organic+</p>
      <h3 id="organic-title" class="mt-1 max-w-3xl text-balance font-display text-h3 font-bold text-foreground">Plan from the trends. Score every hook.</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-[46ch] text-base text-muted-foreground md:mt-3 md:text-lead">Approve a week planned from your market's trends. Every hook is scored against your best posts before you schedule it.</p>
      <div class="sv-settle mt-6 md:mt-8">
        <OrganicDemo client:visible={{ rootMargin: '300px' }} photos={photos} />
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-[80ch] text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
        Plans and previews for Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, TikTok and YouTube. Instagram publishing is live; the other four are built and not yet used in production, so the first post on each goes out supervised with you.
      </p>
      <p class="handoff">Instagram posts that beat your median run as paused Meta ads, likes and comments included.</p>
    </article>

    <article id="performance" class="mt-12 md:mt-28 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="performance-title">
      <p class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-brand-violet">Performance+</p>
      <h3 id="performance-title" class="mt-1 max-w-3xl text-balance font-display text-h3 font-bold text-foreground">The Optimizer proposes. Jaina explains. You approve.</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-[46ch] text-base text-muted-foreground md:mt-3 md:text-lead">Jaina reads your Meta account and answers with the numbers. The Optimizer proposes budget moves inside your caps, and a person approves them. New ads land paused.</p>
      <div class="sv-settle mt-6 md:mt-8">
        <PerformanceDemo client:visible={{ rootMargin: '300px' }} photos={photos} />
      </div>
      <p class="handoff">When creative tires, Jaina can queue a Forge render. It reaches Meta paused, after your sign-off. <span class="pilot">Pilot</span></p>
    </article>

    <article id="automation" class="mt-12 md:mt-28 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="automation-title">
      <p class="font-display text-base font-semibold text-brand-violet">Creative Automation</p>
      <h3 id="automation-title" class="mt-1 max-w-3xl text-balance font-display text-h3 font-bold text-foreground">Your design files in. Paused Meta ads out.</h3>
      <p class="mt-2 max-w-[46ch] text-base text-muted-foreground md:mt-3 md:text-lead">Bring your After Effects project. Forge maps the layers, renders every row in every format, and stages each row on your Meta ad set as a paused ad once you approve.</p>
      <div class="sv-settle mt-6 md:mt-8">
        <AutomationDemo client:visible={{ rootMargin: '300px' }} photos={photos} />
      </div>
      <p class="handoff">The paused ad lands in the account Jaina already reads. The next cycle starts there.</p>
    </article>

    <!-- What a buyer asks before booking: control, brand, setup. Each line is something the app does today. -->
    <div class="mt-12 border-t border-border pt-8 md:mt-24 md:pt-10">
      <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground md:text-2xl">Run it on your own account.</h3>
      <dl class="mt-5 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:gap-10 md:mt-6">
        <div>
          <dt class="inline text-sm font-semibold text-foreground sm:block">Control<span class="sm:hidden">.</span></dt>
          <dd class="inline text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground sm:mt-2 sm:block">Every budget move waits for you, or runs inside your caps on Autopilot <span class="pilot">Pilot</span>. New ads ship paused, and nothing goes live until a person turns it on.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="inline text-sm font-semibold text-foreground sm:block">Brand<span class="sm:hidden">.</span></dt>
          <dd class="inline text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground sm:mt-2 sm:block">Drafts start from your brand book and your best posts. Forge templates come from your own After Effects projects <span class="pilot">Pilot</span>, and a layer it can't map stops and asks.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="inline text-sm font-semibold text-foreground sm:block">Setup<span class="sm:hidden">.</span></dt>
          <dd class="inline text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground sm:mt-2 sm:block">Bring one live Meta campaign. We connect your account with you on the demo.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <a href="/#demo" class="btn-aura btn-aura-day mt-8 h-12 rounded-xl px-7 text-base md:mt-10">Book a demo</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* The thread between chapters: one quiet line saying where the work goes next. */
  .handoff {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    max-width: 48rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    text-indent: -1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--color-muted-foreground);
  }
  .handoff::before { content: "↳"; display: inline-block; width: 1.25rem; text-indent: 0; color: var(--color-brand-violet); }
  /* The app's Preview mark, for capabilities the sales register lists as pilot. */
  .pilot {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-left: 0.375rem;
    text-indent: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 9999px;
    padding: 0.0625rem 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
